    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "Seoul-based illustrator creating narrative-driven architectural comics and artist books; confirmed via Cargo Collective portfolio and It's Nice That feature (Feb 2021). Combines hand-rendered drawing, Xerox processes, and digital editing to make intimate cityscape comics. Published works include Home (2020, 32pp), When We're Not Looking (2019), Pendulum/Sigyechu (2018, autobiographical comic about NYC-Korea journey), There (2017), and House Coloring Book (2017). It's Nice That noted plans to expand into web, motion, and 3D. Contact email hyunminkim111@gmail.com found via IG/Cargo. Clipped only as IG in 2021; site kimhyunmin11.com points to Cargo Collective (domain lapsed). LinkedIn search returned several Hyunmin Kims; could not confirm which (if any) is this illustrator. Autonomy 2: emerging independent illustrator, self-publishes but no major institutional footprint visible; work is strong but relatively underground. Work Status Unknown: no current employer or freelance signal found.",
